course: dictionary
lesson: 6463
title: Born, birth and place: natal
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Natal is an adjective, and it is a formal word, often used in science. It means to do with being born, or with the time of birth. When you meet «natal», ask: what is being born here? The words around it will tell you.
explain: «Take me to my natal shore and the white cliffs of Albion.» The Mariner wants to go back to the place where he was born. Natal means where he was born, so the natal shore is the coast of his birth. Albion is an old name for Britain, and its white cliffs stand at Dover.
explain: Natal also sits inside longer words. Prenatal means before birth, postnatal means after birth, and neonatal means newborn. Once you know natal is about birth, these longer words make more sense.
explain: Natal can also be a place name, with a capital letter. It was the old name of a province of South Africa, now KwaZulu-Natal, and there is a city called Natal in Brazil. A capital letter and a place are your clues that it is a name, not a word about birth.
fact: Natal is an adjective: it describes something to do with being born.
fact: «Natal day» means the day you were born, and «natal home» means the home where you were born.
fact: In biology, a «natal stream» is the river where a salmon hatched, and the salmon returns there to lay its eggs.
fact: Prenatal means before birth, postnatal means after birth, and neonatal means newborn.
fact: Natal with a capital letter is a place name: the old name of a South African province (now KwaZulu-Natal), and a city in Brazil.
exercise: «Take me to my natal shore.» What does natal mean here? | Where you go to school | *Where you were born | Where you buy your food | Where the sea is deepest
exercise: The doctor checked the baby in the prenatal clinic. What does prenatal mean? | *Before birth | Newborn | After birth | In the water
exercise: Which word means newborn? | Prenatal | Natal day | *Neonatal | Postnatal
test: Which one is a place name, not a word about birth? | Natal home | *A city called Natal in Brazil | Natal day | Natal stream
test: What does postnatal mean? | Newborn | Before birth | Very old | *After birth
exam: In «natal day», what does natal tell the reader? | *That the day is about being born | That the day is a place name | That the day is hot | That the day is a holiday
